IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation.
-- LAYER 1, MODULE 1: THE NOUNS.  DECLARE and nothing else: the kinds of thing a witness of ordinary
-- competence could testify to (what was done, what the contract is about, who dealt how).
-- Whether those facts make a term ineffective is a rule, and lives in the module for the section
-- that says so.  Every other module imports this one.
--
-- Source: UCTA1977.txt (a plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text).
-- Target compiler: main (1.6.109).

§ `UCTA - the nouns`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What is relied on to avoid liability (ss 2, 3, 4, 5, 11)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ss 2(1), 2(2), 11(1), 11(3).  The Act speaks of "a contract term" and of "a notice given to persons
-- generally or to particular persons" (s 2(1)), and treats "a notice (not being a notice having
-- contractual effect)" separately (s 11(3)).
DECLARE `What is relied on` IS ONE OF
    `A contract term`
    `A notice that has contractual effect`
    `A notice that does not have contractual effect`

-- ss 2(1), 2(2).  The loss for which liability is said to be excluded or restricted.
DECLARE `Kind of loss` IS ONE OF
    `Death or personal injury`
    `Other loss or damage`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The contract (ss 6, 7, 12(1)(c), 26, Sch 1)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ss 6, 7, 12(1)(c), 26(3)(a).  What kind of contract it is.
DECLARE `Kind of contract` IS ONE OF
    `A contract of sale of goods`
    `A hire-purchase agreement`
    `A contract, not of sale of goods or hire-purchase, under which possession or ownership of goods passes`
    `Another kind of contract`

-- First Schedule paras 1 to 4.  What the contract (or the part of it the term concerns) relates to.
-- Each Schedule paragraph speaks of a contract "so far as it relates" to a subject, so the question
-- is asked of the part of the contract the term is in.
DECLARE `What the contract relates to` IS ONE OF
    `Insurance, including a contract to pay an annuity on human life`
    `The creation, transfer or termination of an interest in land`
    `The creation, transfer or termination of a right or interest in intellectual property`
    `The formation or dissolution of a company, or its constitution or the rights or obligations of its corporators or members`
    `The creation or transfer of securities, or of a right or interest in securities`
    `Marine salvage or towage`
    `A charterparty of a ship or hovercraft`
    `The carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft`
    `Employment`
    `None of these`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What the term does (ss 3, 13)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 3(2).  The three things a party with the benefit of a contract term cannot do as against the
-- party dealing as consumer or on written standard terms, except so far as the term is reasonable.
DECLARE `What a term claims` IS ONE OF
    `Excludes or restricts the other party's liability for its own breach of contract`
    `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected`
    `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation`
    `Something else`

-- s 13(1), (2).  The varieties of exemption clause.
DECLARE `Variety of exemption clause` IS ONE OF
    `Makes the liability or its enforcement subject to restrictive or onerous conditions`
    `Excludes or restricts a right or remedy in respect of the liability, or subjects a person to prejudice for pursuing it`
    `Excludes or restricts rules of evidence or procedure`
    `Excludes or restricts the relevant obligation or duty itself`
    `An agreement in writing to submit present or future differences to arbitration`
    `Another variety`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The undertakings in ss 6 and 7
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 6(1), (2).  The obligations in a sale of goods or hire-purchase.
DECLARE `Obligation in a sale or hire-purchase` IS ONE OF
    `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12`
    `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15`
    `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 section 6`
    `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 section 6A, 6B or 6C`
    `Another obligation`

-- s 7(2), (3), (3A), (4).  The obligations implied by law in another contract under which goods pass.
DECLARE `Obligation in another goods contract` IS ONE OF
    `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample`
    `Quality or fitness of the goods for a particular purpose`
    `Supply of Goods Act 1982 section 2 (implied terms about title)`
    `The right to transfer ownership of the goods, or give possession`
    `The assurance of quiet possession to a person taking the goods`
    `Another obligation`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defined words and the Schedules' tables
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 14, s 29(3), s 1(1), s 12(1), s 5(2).  The words the Act defines.
DECLARE `Defined word` IS ONE OF
    business
    goods
    `hire-purchase agreement`
    negligence
    notice
    `personal injury`
    `competent authority`
    enactment
    statutory
    `deals as consumer`
    `in consumer use`
    guarantee
    `business liability`
    company

-- s 14 and s 29(3): how the Act gives the meaning.
DECLARE `How the Act defines` IS ONE OF
    Means
    Includes
    `Has the same meaning as in another Act`
    `Has the meaning given by a section`
    `Is defined by a list of conditions`

-- A look-up row for a defined word: what the Act itself says.
DECLARE `Definition entry` HAS
    `the word`           IS A `Defined word`
    `section`            IS A STRING
    `how it is defined`  IS A `How the Act defines`
    `what the Act names` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `what it points at`  IS A STRING

-- s 14, "business" includes ...
DECLARE `Kind of activity` IS ONE OF
    `A profession`
    `The activities of a Government department`
    `The activities of a local authority`
    `The activities of a public authority`
    `Another activity`

-- s 14, "personal injury" includes ...
DECLARE `Kind of harm` IS ONE OF
    Death
    `A disease`
    `An impairment of physical or mental condition`
    `A bodily injury`
    `Damage to property or another loss`

-- s 14, "notice" includes ...
DECLARE `Kind of communication` IS ONE OF
    `An announcement, in writing`
    `An announcement, not in writing`
    `Another communication`
    `A pretended communication`
    `Something else`

-- First Schedule para 1(d)(i), "company" means ...
DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `A body corporate`
    `An unincorporated association`
    `A partnership`
    `Something else`

-- s 29(3), "competent authority" means ...
DECLARE `Kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `A court`
    `An arbitrator or arbiter`
    `A Government department`
    `A public authority`
    `Another body`

-- s 29(3), "enactment" means ...
DECLARE `Kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `Legislation of Singapore`
    `Subsidiary legislation of Singapore`
    `An instrument having effect by virtue of legislation of Singapore`
    `Something else`

-- Second Schedule (a) to (e).  The matters to which regard is had in particular.
DECLARE `Guideline` IS ONE OF
    `Bargaining positions and alternative means of meeting the customer's requirements`
    `Inducement, or an opportunity to contract elsewhere without a similar term`
    `Whether the customer knew or ought reasonably to have known of the term`
    `Whether compliance with a condition was practicable`
    `Whether the goods were made, processed or adapted to the customer's special order`

-- s 11(4)(a), (b).  The matters to which regard is had where liability is restricted to a specified sum.
DECLARE `Matter for a capped term` IS ONE OF
    `The resources the party could expect to be available to meet the liability`
    `How far it was open to the party to cover itself by insurance`

-- ss 11(5), 12(3).  Who bears the burden of showing.
DECLARE `Who must show` IS ONE OF
    `Those claiming that the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness`
    `Those claiming that a party does not deal as consumer`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Records of facts (one case is the text's natural unit)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 12(1), (2), (3).  The facts from which "deals as consumer" is worked out.
DECLARE `Dealing facts` HAS
    `the party made the contract in the course of a business`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party held himself or herself out as making the contract in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party made the contract in the course of a business`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `kind of contract`                                                                      IS A `Kind of contract`
    `the goods passing are of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the party is the buyer on a sale by auction or by competitive tender`                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 1(2), s 1(3), First Schedule.  The facts about the case that decide whether sections 2 to 7 reach it.
DECLARE `Scope facts` HAS
    `the liability is business liability`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `kind of contract`                                                                       IS A `Kind of contract`
    `what the contract relates to`                                                           IS A `What the contract relates to`
    `goods are carried by ship or hovercraft under the contract`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract specifies ship or hovercraft as the means of carriage over part of the journey` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract makes no provision as to the means of carriage and does not exclude ship or hovercraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the term operates for and in relation to the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person protected deals as consumer`                                                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the person protected is the employee`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Part 3.  The facts about the case that decide whether ss 26 to 30 take it out of Part 1.
DECLARE `Part 3 facts` HAS
    `the parties have places of business (or, if none, habitual residences) in the territories of different States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods are, when the contract is concluded, in the course of carriage or will be carried from one State to another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acts constituting the offer and acceptance were done in the territories of different States`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract provides for delivery to a State other than the one in which those acts were done`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proper law is the law of Singapore only by choice of the parties`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is for the carriage by sea of a passenger, or of a passenger and luggage`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister's order prescribes this exclusion in these circumstances, to this extent, by this term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the provision is authorised or required by the express terms or necessary implication of an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that instrument`                                                                         IS A `Kind of instrument`
    `the provision was made with a view to compliance with an international agreement to which Singapore is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provision does not operate more restrictively than the agreement contemplates`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the contract was made`                                                          IS A DATE
    `the date the loss or damage was suffered`                                                IS A DATE
    `it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- s 1(2): the answer of the exceptions to which Part 1 is subject, for one section.
--   * "An exception takes the section out of the case": a flat negative of the text does it (the First Schedule's
--     "do not extend to", section 1(3)'s "only to business liability", a Part 3 provision).  The functions in the
--     text's own polarity ("a requirement of reasonableness applies") then answer JUST FALSE; the functions that
--     ask whether the person CAN exclude or rely answer NOTHING (fork F15 in NOTES.md).
--   * "Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told": the removal rests on something the
--     text does not settle (consumer status not known, the Minister's order, section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909);
--     every function answers NOTHING.
DECLARE `Reach of a section` IS ONE OF
    `An exception takes the section out of the case`
    `No exception takes the section out of the case`
    `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told`

-- ss 2 to 7: which section is asked about, for the exceptions that differ by section.
DECLARE `Section of Part 1` IS ONE OF
    `Section 2(1)`
    `Section 2(2)`
    `Section 3`
    `Section 4`
    `Section 5`
    `Section 6`
    `Section 7`

-- s 4(2)(a).
DECLARE `How the liability is incurred` IS ONE OF
    `Directly by the person to be indemnified`
    `Vicariously by the person to be indemnified`
    `In another way`

-- s 4(2)(b).
DECLARE `To whom the liability is owed` IS ONE OF
    `To the person dealing as consumer`
    `To someone else`
